## Key Findings
1. Container creation: `docker run -d` via spawnSync (ADR-006)
2. Mount points: project dir (rw), .tasks/ (rw), .locks/ (rw), ~/.claude (rw), ~/.claude.json (optional)
3. tmpfs: containerHome (/tmp/deckent-home) — Claude CLI needs writable HOME
4. User: run as host uid:gid — blocks root restriction in claude CLI
5. Env injection: HOME, DECKENT_TASK_ID, DECKENT_PROJECT_ROOT, TASK_TIMEOUT, API keys
6. Worker script: .worker-{taskId}.sh written to .tasks/ then executed inside container
7. Claude CLI bootstrap: `claude -p - --model <model> --dangerously-skip-permissions`
8. Heartbeat: background loop every 15s, writes JSON to .tasks/task-{id}.hb
9. EXIT trap: git diff aware — TIMEOUT_WITH_WORK if files changed, NO_GO if not
10. .partial-result: OOM kill safety net written at startup
11. Host-side monitor: docker wait → reconciles exit code with .result selfAssessment
12. Files: .result, .hb, .log, .plan, .partial-result, .timeout, .prompt-*.txt, .worker-*.sh

